# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CONFIT Frontend Client Environment Template (.env.example)
# Client-safe configuration. NEVER place secret provider keys here.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

VITE_APP_NAME="CONFIT"
VITE_API_BASE_URL="/api/v1"
VITE_AI_PROXY_URL="/api/chat"

# Market & Localization defaults: EG (Egypt/EGP), AE (UAE/AED), SA (Saudi/SAR)
VITE_MARKET="EG"
VITE_DEFAULT_LOCALE="en"

# ── Legal / privacy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data-protection contact rendered on /privacy, /terms and /gdpr.
# Leave EMPTY on any deployment that does not actually monitor this mailbox:
# the legal page then states that no mailbox is configured instead of
# publishing an address nobody reads.
VITE_LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL=""

# ── Removed: MediaPipe on-device vision URLs ───────────────────────────────
# These four variables (VITE_MP_WASM / VITE_MP_POSE_URL / VITE_MP_FACE_URL /
# VITE_MP_HAND_URL) were documented here but NEVER read by any file in src/ —
# no source file imports @mediapipe/tasks-vision or fetches a .task model.
# Documenting an on-device inference engine that the product does not ship is
# the same defect class as the footer's withdrawn “On-Device Biometrics”
# claim: it tells a developer or an auditor that biometric processing happens
# locally when in fact the measurement flow compiles SELF-REPORTED inputs
# (see CameraScanModal.runVisionAnalysis) and uploads the photo to the API.
# If on-device inference is ever implemented, re-add the variables together
# with the import that consumes them and the test that proves it runs.

# OIDC Social Client IDs (Public identifiers only)
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
VITE_APPLE_CLIENT_ID=""
VITE_FACEBOOK_CLIENT_ID=""
